\pard\f0\fs28\b SEZOY Privacy Policy\b0\par
\par\pard\f0\fs26\b English\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24\b Privacy Policy\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 \b Last updated:\b0  September 26, 2026\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 1. Information We Collect\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 SEZOY processes information in two different ways:\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab \b Information sent to our server over the Internet:\b0  on the first activation of the software, SEZOY may send a \b device fingerprint\b0  that has been encrypted and truncated. This identifier is used for activation, validation, anti-abuse, and service operation purposes.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab \b Information processed locally only while the software is running:\b0  SEZOY may create and use temporary technical information, interface state, selected device details, ISO selection, edition selection, driver status, software selection, and similar operational values in memory or local runtime state. These values are used only to operate the application while it is open. They are \b not sent to our server over the Internet\b0 , \b not stored on our server\b0 , and are generally cleared when the program is closed unless the user explicitly saves them as part of a local setting or export function.\par
\pard\f0\fs24 When SEZOY applies system-related actions requested by the user, such as adding a certificate to the Trusted Root store or adjusting file sharing-related permissions, those actions are performed locally on the user\u8217?s device. They are configuration changes, not telemetry, and are not transmitted to our server unless a separate online feature explicitly requires it.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 2. How We Use Information\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 We use the information described above to:\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab activate and validate the software;\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab prevent unauthorized use, abuse, or tampering;\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab provide Boot creation, PXE server, ISO integration, driver integration, unattended customization, monitoring, and post-installation workflow features;\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab remember user-selected settings when the product is designed to restore the previous session;\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab display status information and help the user complete the workflow;\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab improve stability, reliability, and compatibility;\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab respond to support requests and troubleshoot issues when the user contacts us.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 3. How We Share Information\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 We do not sell your personal information.\par
\pard\f0\fs24 We may disclose information only in the following cases:\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab \b Service operation:\b0  to process activation or service requests that are required for the software to function.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab \b Legal compliance:\b0  when disclosure is required by law, court order, or a valid government request.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab \b Security and abuse prevention:\b0  when needed to protect the software, our users, or our systems from fraud, misuse, or security threats.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\tx720\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab \b User-directed actions:\b0  when you intentionally download ISO files, drivers, or other packages from third-party providers through the features you choose to use, those providers may receive data according to their own policies.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 4. Third-Party Components and Services\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 SEZOY may include or interact with third-party tools and components such as 7-Zip, aria2, iPXE Bootloaders, busybox, ChromeDriver, erofs-utils, Fido, MSEdgeDriver, noVNC, oscdimg, Ventoy, wimlib, WinCDEmu, and the WinDivert Add-on (optional download for Wi-Fi Hotspot support). Each third-party component remains subject to its own license terms, copyright notices, and usage conditions.\par
\pard\f0\fs24 Some features may require network access to download files or retrieve links from external providers. When you choose such a feature, the relevant provider may process information according to its own privacy policy and terms.\par
\pard\f0\fs24 The WinDivert Add-on (WinDivert driver and pydivert bindings) is not bundled with SEZOY. It is downloaded from its official sources only with your explicit consent and remains governed by its own license terms (LGPLv3).\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 5. Data Retention\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 The device fingerprint sent during first activation may be retained for as long as reasonably necessary to provide activation, validation, fraud prevention, license management, support, or compliance services, and then deleted or irreversibly anonymized when no longer needed, subject to applicable legal obligations.\par
\pard\f0\fs24 Local runtime information that exists only in memory or temporary program state is not kept on our server. Unless you explicitly save a local configuration, export a report, or enable a feature that stores a file on your device, that information normally disappears when the software closes.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 6. Security\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect the information we process. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we aim to reduce risk through access control, limited retention, and feature design.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 7. Your Choices and Controls\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 You may choose whether to use features that require online activation, external downloads, or local system changes. You may also choose which optional settings, ISO files, drivers, and post-installation software are used in a given workflow.\par
\pard\f0\fs24 If you do not want SEZOY to process a device fingerprint for activation, you should not complete the first activation flow.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 8. Children\u8217?s Privacy\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 SEZOY is a technical deployment tool and is not intended as a children\u8217?s service. If you are under the age required by local law to provide consent for online services, you should use the software only with appropriate supervision and permission.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 9. Changes to This Policy\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the software, legal requirements, or data handling practices. The latest version will apply when it is published.\par
\par\pard\f0\fs28\b 10. Contact\b0\par
\pard\f0\fs24 If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how SEZOY handles information, contact TekDT through the official support channel provided with the software.\par
